---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | NoMore5Mins"
  description="How NoMore5Mins handles data: local browser storage for your tools, cookies used by advertising and analytics partners, and your choices."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  h1="Privacy policy"
  intro="Last updated: 26 September 2026"
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information is processed when you use NoMore5Mins (the “site”), why, and what choices
    you have. The short version: your alarms, timers and settings never leave your device; our advertising and
    analytics partners may use cookies as described below.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    The tools save your alarms, timer durations, Pomodoro settings and statistics, world-clock cities, theme and
    language preference in your browser’s <strong>local storage</strong>. This data stays on your device, is not sent
    to us and can be deleted at any time by clearing your browser’s site data.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information we do not collect</h2>
  <p>
    We do not offer accounts and we do not ask for your name, email address or other personal details to use the
    tools. The optional contact form only receives what you choose to type into it.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google AdSense to show ads. Google and its partners use cookies and similar technologies to serve ads based
    on your prior visits to this and other websites, to limit how often you see an ad and to measure ad performance.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet.</li>
    <li>You can opt out of personalised advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of some third-party vendors’ use of cookies at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener">aboutads.info</a> and <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="nofollow noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</li>
    <li>Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent through a
    Google-certified consent management platform before personalised ads or non-essential cookies are used. You can
    change your choice at any time via the privacy settings link shown by that platform.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We may use privacy-friendly analytics (such as Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies) and/or
    Google Analytics 4 to understand which tools are used and to fix problems. Analytics data is aggregated; IP
    addresses are not used to identify you. Where consent is required, Google Analytics only runs after you give it.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    NoMore5Mins is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program and other Amazon affiliate programs,
    advertising programs designed to provide a means for sites to earn fees by linking to Amazon. When you click an
    Amazon link, Amazon may set cookies to attribute a purchase to us. We do not receive any information about you or
    your purchases.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Notifications, sound and screen wake lock</h2>
  <p>
    If you allow notifications, alarms and timers can show a system notification. Permission is handled entirely by
    your browser and no notification data is sent to us. The screen wake lock only keeps your display on while a tool
    is running.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Hosting and logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by a static hosting / CDN provider, which may process technical data such as IP address, user
    agent and requested URL in server logs for security and reliability, typically for a short period.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR or the CCPA/CPRA) you may have the right to access,
    correct, delete or object to the processing of personal data, and to withdraw consent. Because we do not hold
    personal data about visitors, most requests are best directed to the providers named above; you can also
    <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> and we will help.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>The site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest revision.</p>
</PageLayout>
